FaceShatter 🧩 — AI-Powered Face Puzzle Game
Day 20 of my 60-Day Claude AI Challenge 🚀
A single-file, dark-themed photo puzzle game built entirely with HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript — no frameworks, no build step. Snap a photo (or load a demo image), choose your difficulty, and solve your own face as a sliding puzzle — right in the browser.
✨ Features
📸 Camera capture — live webcam preview with getUserMedia(), square-cropped snapshot onto canvas
🧩 3 difficulty levels — 3×3, 4×4, or 5×5 grids, sliced dynamically from the captured image
🎲 Guaranteed-solvable shuffle — randomized piece placement, never starts pre-solved
🖱️ Full drag & drop — mouse support for desktop and native touch support for mobile/tablet
🎯 Smart swapping — drag a piece onto another to swap instantly, with snap-to-grid placement
🟢 Live correctness feedback — pieces glow green the moment they land in the right spot
⏱️ Live timer + move counter — mm:ss.t precision timing, move count, and correct-piece tracker
🏆 Win detection + leaderboard — auto-detects completion, stores your top 5 best times in localStorage with date, moves, and difficulty
📱 Fully responsive — clean glassmorphism UI that adapts from desktop to mobile
🔁 Retake / Reshuffle / New Photo / Play Again controls built in
🎨 Design
Theme: Dark violet/indigo SaaS aesthetic with glassmorphism panels
Typography: Space Grotesk (display) + JetBrains Mono (data/labels)
Signature touch: animated "scan line" flash on photo capture, soft glow on correctly placed pieces
🛠️ Tech Stack
100% vanilla HTML / CSS / JavaScript — zero dependencies, zero build tools
getUserMedia() for camera access
HTML5 <canvas> for image capture and slicing
localStorage for persistent leaderboard
Mouse + Touch event handling for cross-device drag and drop
🚀 Run It
Download face-puzzle.html
Open it in any modern browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari)
Camera requires HTTPS or localhost — works out of the box if opened locally or hosted
Allow camera access → take a photo → pick difficulty → solve!
No installs. No servers. No nonsense.
